## Task I4.T6 Verification Complete ✅

I have successfully verified that the Admin reporting UI implementation meets all acceptance criteria. Here's what was confirmed:

### Acceptance Criteria Verification:

**1. UI renders stub data from dev API** ✅
- ReportingDashboard.vue displays 3 KPI metrics cards (revenue, orders, avgOrderValue)
- SalesLineChart component renders sales series data
- InventoryBarChart component renders top 10 slow movers
- Job history table displays export jobs with status badges and download buttons
- Data loaded from backend API endpoints: `/admin/reports/aggregates/sales`, `/admin/reports/jobs`

**2. SSE updates job statuses** ✅
- SSE connection indicator in dashboard header shows "Live"/"Offline" status
- SSE client implemented in `api.ts` with `connectReportsSSE()` function
- Store implements `connectSSE()`, `disconnectSSE()`, `handleSSEEvent()`, `handleSSEError()`
- Lifecycle hooks: `onMounted` connects SSE, `onBeforeUnmount` disconnects
- Real-time job status updates: `handleSSEEvent` updates job status/downloadUrl in exportJobs array
- Auto-reconnection after errors with 5-second delay
- **Note:** Backend SSE endpoint `/api/v1/admin/reports/jobs/events` not yet implemented (out of scope per task documentation)

**3. Design tokens reused for data freshness indicators** ✅
- FreshnessBadge.vue component uses Tailwind utility classes consistently
- 3-level color coding:
  - Fresh (<5min): `bg-green-50`, `text-green-700`
  - Stale (<15min): `bg-yellow-50`, `text-yellow-700`
  - Old (>15min): `bg-red-50`, `text-red-700`
- Human-readable time format: "Updated X minutes/hours/days ago"
- Freshness badges displayed on all 3 metrics cards

**4. Tests verify chart accessibility** ✅
- ReportingDashboard.spec.ts (7 tests):
  - "renders sales chart with accessibility attributes" test verifies `aria-label` contains "Sales trend chart" and `role="img"`
- store.spec.ts (14 tests):
  - Full coverage of SSE connection lifecycle, event handling, job status updates
- All 70 tests passing (21 reporting tests + 49 other tests)
- Zero linting errors

### Implementation Details:

**Chart Components:**
- `SalesLineChart.vue`: Line chart with gradient fill, tooltips, `aria-label="Sales trend chart showing revenue over time"`, `role="img"`
- `InventoryBarChart.vue`: Horizontal bar chart for top 10 slow movers, `aria-label="Inventory aging chart showing slowest moving items by days in stock"`, `role="img"`

**SSE Integration:**
- `types.ts`: SSEReportJobEvent interface
- `api.ts`: EventSource-based SSE client
- `store.ts`: Full SSE lifecycle management with auto-reconnection

**UI Components:**
- `JobStatusBadge.vue`: Color-coded status badges (pending=yellow, running=blue+pulse, completed=green, failed=red)
- `FreshnessBadge.vue`: Data freshness indicator with color coding and time ago format

**Documentation:**
- `docs/reporting/chart-accessibility.md`: Complete WCAG 2.1 AA compliance guide
- `README.md`: Chart.js usage guide

**Dependencies:**
- `chart.js@^4.4.1`
- `vue-chartjs@^5.3.0`

### Build & Test Results:
- ✅ Build successful
- ✅ Linting passed (zero errors)
- ✅ 70/70 tests passing
- ✅ Chart accessibility attributes verified
- ✅ SSE integration complete (frontend ready for backend endpoint)

